WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.914
You already know this part.

2
00:00:01.914 --> 00:00:06.039
The model reads your prompt and scores
every token in its vocabulary.

3
00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:09.690
A decision model stops right here.

4
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.940
Instead of sampling, it takes three rows:
the tokens A, B and C.

5
00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:19.265
Then it renormalises over just those
three.

6
00:00:19.265 --> 00:00:22.867
Subtract the max, exponentiate, divide by
the sum.

7
00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:24.956
That is the entire mechanism.

8
00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:28.818
So your options are only text in the
prompt.

9
00:00:28.818 --> 00:00:32.932
Reverse the list, and nearly twenty-eight
percent of decisions change.

10
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.105
The other family has no vocabulary at all.

11
00:00:38.105 --> 00:00:41.444
Its head outputs a single number, once per
option.

12
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:48.591
So N is a loop bound, not a weight, and
there are no letters for a prior to attach to.
